{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"antitoxic-malophilic-starling","creation_channel":"cli","description":"docker-storage-cap.sh picks the \"modern\" builder.gc schema at BuildKit >= 0.13 and writes builder.gc.maxUsedSpace directly under gc. Two sources disagree with that:\n- BuildKit v0.17.0 release notes (PRs #5359, #5079) are where reserved and maximum storage limits first appear, so 0.13 to 0.16 builders would get a key they do not implement. That is the same silent no-op as catty-giddied-hedgehog, one version band higher.\n- The current dockerd reference example shows maxUsedSpace only INSIDE builder.gc.policy[] entries. The only space key it shows directly under gc is defaultReservedSpace, so gc-level maxUsedSpace may be ignored even on Engine 28+ (BuildKit 0.20).\nNot live on rebar-gerrit, which runs BuildKit 0.12.6 and takes the legacy defaultKeepStorage branch. Unverified: the moby daemon config struct for Engine 28 gc-level keys. Next check: read moby daemon/config BuilderGCConfig at v28.0.0, then pin the schema boundary and key placement with tests in tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py.\nFound 2026-11-03 while working alchemic-ornate-eider (session a85e3cd3).","id":"5bc1-7e5b-3b4c-46c8","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"docker-storage-cap modern GC schema may write an ignored key"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793753553116698001,"uuid":"7cbb466f-423e-458e-8b81-04066d794ddd"}